{"name":"Parsnip","hex":"#d6c69a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parsnip","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A biennial plant, Pastinaca sativa, related to the carrot.","The root of the parsnip, when used as a vegetable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parsnip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parsnip","blocks":[{"text":"The parsnip is a root vegetable closely related to carrot and parsley, all belonging to the flowering plant family Apiaceae. It is a biennial plant usually grown as an annual. Its long taproot has light cream colored skin and flesh, and, left in the ground to mature, becomes sweeter in flavor after winter frosts. In its first growing season, the plant has a rosette of pinnate, mid-green leaves. If unharvested, it produces a flowering stem topped by an umbel of small yellow flowers in its second growing season, later producing pale brown, flat, winged seeds. By this time, the stem has become woody, and the taproot inedible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Pastinaca_sativa_MHNT.BOT.2004.0.jpg/330px-Pastinaca_sativa_MHNT.BOT.2004.0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parsnip","wikidata":"Q188614"},{"title":"Parsnip (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Parsnip is an Australian rock band. They released their debut album, When the Tree Bears Fruit in 2019 with the line-up of Carolyn Hawkins on drums, Stella Rennex on guitar and vocals, Paris Richenson bass guitar and vocals and Rebecca Liston on keyboards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Parsnip_at_Rod_Laver_Arena._Photo_by_Jamie_Wdziekonski.jpg/330px-Parsnip_at_Rod_Laver_Arena._Photo_by_Jamie_Wdziekonski.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parsnip_(band)","wikidata":"Q111992511"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb